<title>RUSSIA: Russian H1 oil output stabilises at 147 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russian H1 oil output stabilises at 147 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian crude oil output appears to have finally stabilised after years of decline, with output over the first half of 1997 at 147 million tonnes, or about 5.88 million barrels per day, official figures showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>The State Statistics Committee released the following data:</p>
<p>			 RUSSIAN H1 97 ENERGY OUTPUT</p>
<p>		(in million tonnes, except where indicated)</p>
<p>			 H1 97    pct change   June 97 as pct</p>
<p>				    yr/yr	  of June 96</p>
<p>Electricity	  423	-4	     -2</p>
<p>(billion kilowatt hours)</p>
<p>Crude oil	    147	+0.4	   +1</p>
<p>Primary processing  87.4    -2	     +5</p>
<p>Gasoline		13.2    -1	     +2</p>
<p>Diesel fuel	   23.4    -1	     +5</p>
<p>Heavy fuel oil	31.9    -3	     +8</p>
<p>Natural gas	  282	-5	    -12</p>
<p>(billion cubic meters)</p>
<p>Coal		   125	-7	     -7</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
